{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion","id":1508432,"title":"Weapons and Explosives discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-15T05:51:31-07:00","id":1508432,"title":"Weapons and Explosives discussion","content":"reading hurt locker (but the same applies to the core also) I have some concern about the weapons' design and explosive damage output:<br /> <br /> 1. I see a bit weak how Blunt and Bladed weapons are designed and differentiated. To me, bladed weapons should still do respectively lethal and bashing damages as it was in 1st edition and the two types of weapons should be differentiated in a different way. as an example, I would have a sledgehammer dealing a bit more damage than a two handed sword (due to the weight) but still bashing, with the knockdown and stun tags as it's now. I'm really not convinced that a metal club should be as lethal as a machete. Can for sure be more efficient to stun the target but I see machete still more deadly in the very meaning of this word. What's your opinion on this? Are you adopting any house-rule to deal with this?<br /> <br /> 2. If I got correctly how explosives works seems to me they are to weak in their damage output. Let's take heavy Frag grenade as an example: it deals +3 damage and has force of 3. Let's take the target - a normal average mortal (7 - 8 health) - being at ground zero, holding the grenade in his very hands. He will suffer 3 aggravated damages + the successes rolled on 4 dice (let's consider 2 damages more). He will eventually suffers 5 aggravated damages staying still alive. I feel that a Frag Grenade at ground zero should kills 99% of human beings ripping them apart, which does not the case here. I still do like the design of downgrading the damages with the 3 blast areas but the raw damage should be fine tuned to me. I would at least double the damage or - at the very least - double the force value o giving it the 8'again quality. <br /> <br /> Any thought?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T06:50:51-07:00","id":1508438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion#post1508432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. If I got correctly how explosives works seems to me they are to weak in their damage output. Let's take heavy Frag grenade as an example: it deals +3 damage and has force of 3. Let's take the target - a normal average mortal (7 - 8 health) - being at ground zero, holding the grenade in his very hands. He will suffer 3 aggravated damages + the successes rolled on 4 dice (let's consider 2 damages more). He will eventually suffers 5 aggravated damages staying still alive. I feel that a Frag Grenade at ground zero should kills 99% of human beings ripping them apart, which does not the case here. I still do like the design of downgrading the damages with the 3 blast areas but the raw damage should be fine tuned to me. I would at least double the damage or - at the very least - double the force value o giving it the 8'again quality.<br /> <br /> Any thought?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the grenades add their damage again on a successful roll so in your example the person would take 6 aggravated damage, not 5. I could be misunderstanding how explosives do damage though. <br /> <br /> Personally, I think that's enough. This game is a storytelling game, not a war simulator. &quot;Bang, you're dead&quot; is virtually never a good story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T06:53:58-07:00","id":1508439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion#post1508432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I see a bit weak how Blunt and Bladed weapons are designed and differentiated. To me, bladed weapons should still do respectively lethal and bashing damages as it was in 1st edition and the two types of weapons should be differentiated in a different way. as an example, I would have a sledgehammer dealing a bit more damage than a two handed sword (due to the weight) but still bashing, with the knockdown and stun tags as it's now. I'm really not convinced that a metal club should be as lethal as a machete. Can for sure be more efficient to stun the target but I see machete still more deadly in the very meaning of this word. What's your opinion on this? Are you adopting any house-rule to deal with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the rules for Beaten Down and Pulling Blows and the rest of the mechanics around Intent and losing Willpower from unintended killing, I feel like the fact that a metal club is as useful as a machete for ending a fight nonlethally while also being optimally more vicious in how one can best use it to kill someone in a fight is a feature, not a bug \u2014 narratively, one does not take a full swing to the arm with a hunk of metal and come back totally fine three hours later without medical treatment or supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. If I got correctly how explosives works seems to me they are to weak in their damage output. Let's take heavy Frag grenade as an example: it deals +3 damage and has force of 3. Let's take the target - a normal average mortal (7 - 8 health) - being at ground zero, holding the grenade in his very hands. He will suffer 3 aggravated damages + the successes rolled on 4 dice (let's consider 2 damages more). He will eventually suffers 5 aggravated damages staying still alive. I feel that a Frag Grenade at ground zero should kills 99% of human beings ripping them apart, which does not the case here. I still do like the design of downgrading the damages with the 3 blast areas but the raw damage should be fine tuned to me. I would at least double the damage or - at the very least - double the force value o giving it the 8'again quality.<br /> <br /> Any thought? </div> </div> </div>A heavy frag grenade has a Damage rating of +3 and a Force rating of 4. At ground zero, this means a person takes three aggravated damage, and if the Force roll succeeds it adds the successes on that roll <i>plus the Damage rating again</i> to that aggravated damage. That means a successful full hit with a heavy frag grenade deals <i>at least seven</i> aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Fixed so that stats for the heavy frag grenade are cited instead of stats for the standard frag grenade. 04-15-2023, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T04:23:57-07:00","id":1508523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion?p=1508439#post1508439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between the rules for Beaten Down and Pulling Blows and the rest of the mechanics around Intent and losing Willpower from unintended killing, I feel like the fact that a metal club is as useful as a machete for ending a fight nonlethally while also being optimally more vicious in how one can best use it to kill someone in a fight is a feature, not a bug \u2014 narratively, one does not take a full swing to the arm with a hunk of metal and come back totally fine three hours later without medical treatment or supernatural powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that a broken arm should not get recovered in a matters of hours and yet I feel like having several bones got broken by a club is still less life-threatening than the same amount of damage done by a sword. The difference, in my opinion, relies on the fact that I could beat down an enemy with a club leaving him with several broken ribs and bones OR dead. For a mortal this makes a huge difference actually.<br /> A way to solve this could be using tilts; something like: all blunt weapons that deals more damages than stamina in a single attack do inflict a &quot;broken bone&quot; tilt which, if not affecting a specific limb - in which case it cause the already described tilts for that specific limb, it lead to a generic -2 penalty (on top of the health boxes penalties - e.g.: some broken ribs) which recovers in 10-stamina weeks.<br /> <br /> Like it is now I really can't see the great innovation which brought humanity to develop always sharper blades. It's true that in battlefields also hammers, maces etc were used, but for a different reason: to smash through armors, and anyway the vast majority of those were anyway with some spike(s).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion?p=1508439#post1508439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A heavy frag grenade has a Damage rating of +3 and a Force rating of 4. At ground zero, this means a person takes three aggravated damage, and if the Force roll succeeds it adds the successes on that roll <i>plus the Damage rating again</i> to that aggravated damage. That means a successful full hit with a heavy frag grenade deals <i>at least seven</i> aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right. I completely missed the part where it's stated that the damage is applied again. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T10:01:25-07:00","id":1508538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1508432-weapons-and-explosives-discussion?p=1508523#post1508523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A way to solve this could be using tilts; something like: all blunt weapons that deals more damages than stamina in a single attack do inflict a &quot;broken bone&quot; tilt which, if not affecting a specific limb - in which case it cause the already described tilts for that specific limb, it lead to a generic -2 penalty (on top of the health boxes penalties - e.g.: some broken ribs) which recovers in 10-stamina weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that the default system for recovering from Tilts caused by damage is predicated on healing all the damage that caused the Tilt and taking seven weeks for a person with above-average Stamina to recover from a Personal Tilt over time would be equivalent to recovering from seven points of aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Hurt Locker's section on Lasting Trauma discusses the fact that ChroD takes a charitable approach to injury and provides some alternatives that may work for your purposes, as might the Conditions-As-Health Twist from VtR 2e Core, but as it stands dealing lethal damage and attached Tilts/Conditions is the primary way the system models injury that lasts beyond a scene or two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T17:00:28-07:00","id":1508585,"title":"","content":"Also I think the Bleeding Tilt basically covers your concerns about bladed weapons. A regular longsword deals at least 4 damage which would inflict Bleeding on most ordinary characters. They now suffer an extra 1 to Wound Penalties and take a Bashing damage each turn. Even assuming no other damage (unlikely since there's a guy trying to murder them with a sword), they will begin to risk passing out in a few turns and if they do pass out will bleed out in a minute or two unless someone else stems the bleeding.<br /> <br /> I'd also try not to get hung up in the actual words 'bashing' and 'lethal' which really just reflect abstract tiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27690-morgang","name":"MorganG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-16T21:23:39-07:00","id":1508601,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not sure that being whacked with a stout club is any less life threatening then getting a cut from a sword or knife. It's a different kind of damage, but not what bashing damage seems designed to represent.<br /> <br /> Honestly if there is ever a CofD3 maybe they should rename Bashing damage to Minor damage or the like (Superficial? Incidental?).<br /> <br /> It also has the rather nice benefit of pushing characters away from the old trenchcoat+katana model and towards blunt weapons they can more reasonably justify having in their bag or the boot of their car (especially if you're playing in a country where firearms are more regulated). Not there shouldn't be characters who carry knives, but wrecking bars and cricket bats should probably be more common than rapiers and wakizashi (unless playing in an appropriate historical setting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}